=== Allow wp-admin access ===

Contributors: brainvireinfo
Tags: allow ip, restrict wp-admin, restrict wp-admin using ip, restrict admin
Requires at least: 4.0.0
Tested up to: 6.7.1
Stable tag: 1.0.3
License: GPLv2 or later
License URI: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html

The plugin enable the admin users to allow admin access whose IP address is mentioned in the “WP-admin Access Allow Settings.”

== Description ==
Admin can manage “Allow Wp-Admin Access” from a single or multiple IP address. It is helpful when the website is in development mode or to keep the website secure, so nobody can access the admin panel.

= How is it Useful? =

* You can give access of wp-admin to a particular IP address
* You can check which IP address is accessible from wp-admin
* You can make the website login secured using IP address 
* You can avoid spam IP address   

== Installation ==

how to install the plugin and get it working.

e.g.

1. Upload plugin to the `/wp-content/plugins/` directory
2. Activate the plugin through the 'Plugins' menu in WordPress

